						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">I&#039;ll go off my experience and thoughts.<br /><br />What VM (Quellious Guild) from my personal knowledge of the subject was an &#039;ok&#039; way to deal with the situation.  I think that being in different high end guilds if you&#039;re married, in a relationship or what have you is a conflict of interest.  It&#039;s up to the parties involved on how to deal with it however.  I feel strats are a very personal thing to a guild, if VM had the notion that their strats were being used by other guilds then yes they are well within their &#039;rights&#039; of fixing the problem.<br /><br />Taking an extension of that point, and your discussion of &#039;getting info from other guilds&#039;.  Honsetly it happens.  I&#039;m probably the most active DA/EiE person on our current stratagies and I&#039;ll tell you now I dont send 54 people in right away not knowing anything about an encounter.<br /><br />My method basically would go through what I&#039;d consider five phases.<br /><br />#1 I go to Allakazam and see what AE&#039;s are listed.<br />#2 I go to Lucy to find the effects of the AE<br />#3 I ask around to find melee DPS to decide CH Chain Strength<br />#4 I download a Map and decide best positioning.<br />#5 I fill in the gaps<br /><br />If anyone denies talking to other guilds, other friends then they&#039;re an outright liar.  When SoE designs content there is always &#039;1&#039; way to deal with it.  That 1 way has about 100 different variations (all minor) but there truly is 1 vision.<br /><br />Going off what Justyse said, it is very much the same with DA/EiE.  DA/EiE has forever been a high druid, medium cleric guild.  The cleric class is the backbone of your raid force, as such you depend and rely on them for alot of your needs.  Most top end guilds average about 10-12 clerics (because of bots) which we simply do not field.  We on average field from 7-10 along with 4-8 druids (most guilds use 2-4 I&#039;d say).<br /><br />That restricts, yet opens up alot of options for us as a guild on how to do things.<br /><br />I dont think alot of guilds are delivered a complete strat, nor do I think any guilds that have them even use them.. but every guild or raid leader walks into an encounter knowing what he or she is up against (unless you are literally doing it for the 1st time).<br /></td>
