						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">Rather then doing a long post (which I just deleted in the saving of drama) I&#039;ll just say some general comments.<br /><br />To Anyone that needed the loot:<br /><br />I&#039;m sorry.  It was never my intention to &#039;cockblock&#039; you from the loot which would&#039;ve been gained from the event.<br /><br />To People that think it was an asshole thing to do:<br /><br />I&#039;m not sorry.  Anyone that knows me to a decent degree knows I love to push the envelope in content.  If that means boxing a Msha in Qvic, or boxing a Fennin Ro trigger that is regardless.  In this case sadly loot was lost for some other players.<br /><br />To the People that think there was no reason to kill the trigger:<br /><br />There were two reasons to do so.<br /><br />#1 I got experience from the kill.  This played about 0% into the debate of if my group should kill it or not.<br />#2 My group did intend to actually finish through the entire script.  However I did not know about the concentration of mobs for the initial pull (the demon surrounded by like 8 (?) guards).  I did not have the pull team required to do that, so I decided to leave after attempts failed and pulling them out.  Yes we stayed for more then &quot;1 minute.&quot;&nbsp; The goal in my mind was to do two things really:<br /><br />1.&nbsp; Open up mobs that would have no competition over.<br />2.&nbsp; Get to F Ro and box him.&nbsp; <br /><br />Being unable to pull stopped that rather quickly.&nbsp; As such we decided to leave as we were running very low on mobs.<br /><br />To Kinsonn:<br /><br />Grow up.  Attacking people in rude means does you nothing.<br /><br />Once again to those that would&#039;ve received loot I am sorry.<br /><br /></td>
